%description:

Tcp.alignOptions:aligned -- NOP options align the options of a segment.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "align each TCP option with NOP options before it".

The classes: aligned (true, the default), packed (false). The code: the NOP before each option
(TcpConnection::addSacks() and the options of the SYN). This test separates "aligned" from "packed".

Host under test: host1. Observation: level 1, the SYN of host1 has NOP options.

%# parameter: Tcp.alignOptions
%# class: aligned
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.alignOptions
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlignOptionsAligned")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpOptionCount(context.event.packet, inet::tcp::TCPOPTION_NO_OPERATION) > 0; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with NOP options")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlignOptionsAligned compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.alignOptions = true    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlignOptionsAligned: PASS
